From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:37:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] End when the terminal's input fails or closes instead of
 panicking

Problem: when the terminal goes away while Helix runs (on AROS: the Limpet
window is closed), the input stream yields an error (UnexpectedEof), and
handle_terminal_events unwraps it: the editor thread panics. Other input
errors (a failed poll or read) end the same way.
Change: an error from the terminal's input ends the event loop, as a
hang-up does; the terminal is restored if it can be, and Helix exits.
Unsaved changes are lost, as with SIGHUP on other systems. An interrupted
read (which the event stream does not pass on today) is ignored.
Repository: helix-editor/helix
Base: a05c151bb6e8e9c65ec390b0ae2afe7a5efd619b (tag 25.07.1)
Author: tomaszstaniak
Date: 2026-10-19
Platform scope: all targets.
Upstream status: candidate (not submitted).
Verification: on AROS One 1.3, closing the Limpet 0.6.1 window while hx runs
ends hx and the window closes; before, the window stayed on "Closing:
waiting for process". Host: cargo check.
---
 helix-term/src/application.rs | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/helix-term/src/application.rs b/helix-term/src/application.rs
index 40faf2fb61a8cb31cf0f15dabf4e10689016f9a2..97f8e8b4aff388d56c23bcc9cdf8fef52876c09d 100644
--- a/helix-term/src/application.rs
+++ b/helix-term/src/application.rs
@@ -315,7 +315,17 @@ pub async fn event_loop_until_idle<S>(&mut self, input_stream: &mut S) -> bool
                     };
                 }
                 Some(event) = input_stream.next() => {
-                    self.handle_terminal_events(event).await;
+                    // The terminal's input failed or ended (its window was
+                    // closed): end as after a hang-up instead of panicking
+                    // on the error. Only an interrupted read is retried.
+                    if let Err(err) = &event {
+                        if err.kind() != std::io::ErrorKind::Interrupted {
+                            log::info!("terminal input failed ({err}), quitting");
+                            return false;
+                        }
+                    } else {
+                        self.handle_terminal_events(event).await;
+                    }
                 }
                 Some(callback) = self.jobs.callbacks.recv() => {
                     self.jobs.handle_callback(&mut self.editor, &mut self.compositor, Ok(Some(callback)));
